WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.457 --> 00:00:02.149
- I watched, I think at the time,

00:00:02.149 --> 00:00:04.361
like every single coming
out video on YouTube.

00:00:04.361 --> 00:00:08.129
Hearing their stories and
everything comforted me so much.

00:00:08.129 --> 00:00:10.567
There are so many people
that I could like,

00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:13.572
really, really, I would love
to meet and say thank you to.

00:00:13.572 --> 00:00:16.155
(upbeat music)

00:00:20.609 --> 00:00:23.224
I do like 10 push ups,
sometimes I'll do star jumps too

00:00:23.224 --> 00:00:25.891
if I'm feeling like a bit crazy.

00:00:30.322 --> 00:00:32.712
The first one that actually mattered to me

00:00:32.712 --> 00:00:36.366
who has like since come out as
not straight is Miley Cyrus.

00:00:36.366 --> 00:00:38.890
I remember she, when I
was like 13 or whatever

00:00:38.890 --> 00:00:40.319
and watching Hannah Montana,

00:00:40.319 --> 00:00:42.249
I thought she was like the
coolest person in the world,

00:00:42.249 --> 00:00:44.558
and she wrote a song called
My Heart Beats For Love,

00:00:44.558 --> 00:00:45.611
she said in an interview that it was about

00:00:45.611 --> 00:00:46.884
her gay best friend,

00:00:46.884 --> 00:00:49.754
and I was like oh my God, Miley
Cyrus has a gay best friend.

00:00:49.754 --> 00:00:51.349
Why am I not that person?

00:00:51.349 --> 00:00:53.689
And I was like, if everyone
in the world rejects me

00:00:53.689 --> 00:00:57.522
I can just go become
friends with Miley Cyrus.

00:00:59.218 --> 00:01:02.631
I would say, try not to stress.

00:01:02.631 --> 00:01:04.146
I know that that is like,

00:01:04.146 --> 00:01:06.318
it seems like such a silly thing to say,

00:01:06.318 --> 00:01:09.327
but really, there are people in the world

00:01:09.327 --> 00:01:13.494
who 1000% will love you
like just the way you are.

00:01:16.381 --> 00:01:18.146
It came about with,
Alessia and I were mates,

00:01:18.146 --> 00:01:20.094
and we had met a couple of times,

00:01:20.094 --> 00:01:22.506
and I covered her song Here on the radio,

00:01:22.506 --> 00:01:25.175
and then she covered my
song Youth on the radio,

00:01:25.175 --> 00:01:26.368
and I texted her and I was like,

00:01:26.368 --> 00:01:27.977
okay well I'm gonna one up you and cover,

00:01:27.977 --> 00:01:30.259
I think I threatened her with Wild Things,

00:01:30.259 --> 00:01:31.659
and she was like, well no,

00:01:31.659 --> 00:01:32.833
let's do something official,

00:01:32.833 --> 00:01:34.166
and I was like, sweet let's do it,

00:01:34.166 --> 00:01:34.999
and she went into the studio,

00:01:34.999 --> 00:01:36.294
and she recorded her verse on Wild,

00:01:36.294 --> 00:01:38.294
and I like lost my mind.

00:01:40.829 --> 00:01:42.999
I can't commit to anything stylistically

00:01:42.999 --> 00:01:44.256
for the rest of my life,

00:01:44.256 --> 00:01:47.102
so I would just get probably
super, super simple,

00:01:47.102 --> 00:01:50.014
my family's names or initials,

00:01:50.014 --> 00:01:51.931
or something like that.

00:01:55.455 --> 00:01:57.992
The only way that I knew
I was ready to come out

00:01:57.992 --> 00:02:01.367
was I was being driven crazy
by the fact that I was not out.

00:02:01.367 --> 00:02:04.671
Every single time I was alone
with either of my parents

00:02:04.671 --> 00:02:05.702
for a split second I was like,

00:02:05.702 --> 00:02:06.926
oh my God, am I gonna do it now,

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:07.759
is this the time?

00:02:07.759 --> 00:02:09.835
How can I get the
conversation to go there?

00:02:09.835 --> 00:02:11.683
And it was literally driving me insane,

00:02:11.683 --> 00:02:12.618
I thought I was going nuts.

00:02:12.618 --> 00:02:14.621
It's so weird, 'cause
it's one of those things

00:02:14.621 --> 00:02:15.655
that you build up, you know,

00:02:15.655 --> 00:02:17.657
I had built this up for
like 15 years in my head,

00:02:17.657 --> 00:02:21.240
and then it's like two
words and it's over.

00:02:23.105 --> 00:02:27.105
Always put ketchup on my
mac and cheese, always.

00:02:31.182 --> 00:02:33.943
I think I have to kind of
be aware of how much power

00:02:33.943 --> 00:02:35.175
words can have,

00:02:35.175 --> 00:02:37.973
and yeah, it makes me
consider everything that I say

00:02:37.973 --> 00:02:38.981
before I say it,

00:02:38.981 --> 00:02:40.887
because yeah, you know,

00:02:40.887 --> 00:02:43.462
you can really help a lot of people,

00:02:43.462 --> 00:02:45.169
or you can really, really mess things up,

00:02:45.169 --> 00:02:49.002
and so, yeah just try
to be smart and helpful.

00:02:52.037 --> 00:02:53.616
Firstly, ask his permission I recon,

00:02:53.616 --> 00:02:55.143
and then, I mean, if he's down,

00:02:55.143 --> 00:02:56.060
go all out,

00:02:57.985 --> 00:03:00.143
pride flags, glitter,
obviously the playlist

00:03:00.143 --> 00:03:01.808
is very important too,

00:03:01.808 --> 00:03:03.641
like a lot of Madonna.

00:03:06.583 --> 00:03:10.839
I love when people make like
these collaborative books.

00:03:10.839 --> 00:03:13.593
I get these booklets, and
it's letters from a bunch

00:03:13.593 --> 00:03:14.800
of different people,

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:18.130
and they warm my heart so much.

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:22.297
I love, love, love reading
them on the tour bus and stuff.

00:03:23.185 --> 00:03:25.435
It's on my right, this one.

00:03:29.048 --> 00:03:30.720
Definitely the writing, yeah.

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:33.043
I love, love, love,
love, love songwriting,

00:03:33.043 --> 00:03:35.145
and that whole, you know,

00:03:35.145 --> 00:03:36.963
I don't know, for me it's
like the most therapeutic

00:03:36.963 --> 00:03:38.546
thing in the world.

00:03:41.346 --> 00:03:45.251
I didn't realize how much
me hiding my sexuality

00:03:45.251 --> 00:03:48.371
also meant that I hid like
a lot of just my identity

00:03:48.371 --> 00:03:49.204
as a person.

00:03:49.204 --> 00:03:51.441
I think I realize now I
was really, really scared

00:03:51.441 --> 00:03:55.055
to you know, express
myself to like fashion,

00:03:55.055 --> 00:03:56.201
or like certain music,

00:03:56.201 --> 00:03:57.534
or like certain TV shows.

00:03:57.534 --> 00:03:59.927
I was petrified that anyone
would ever think I was gay,

00:03:59.927 --> 00:04:03.173
God forbid, and so once I got over that

00:04:03.173 --> 00:04:06.090
I kind of could just let myself be.

00:04:07.320 --> 00:04:09.490
I realized that yeah, it gets,

00:04:09.490 --> 00:04:11.715
you know, I'm kind of a different person

00:04:11.715 --> 00:04:13.029
than I thought I was.

00:04:13.029 --> 00:04:13.862
Bye.

